NNAAMMEE
     ffwwiiddee — get/set orientation of a stream

LLIIBBRRAARRYY
     Standard C Library (libc, -lc)

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ##iinncclluuddee <<ssttddiioo..hh>>
     ##iinncclluuddee <<wwcchhaarr..hh>>

     _i_n_t
     ffwwiiddee(_F_I_L_E _*_s_t_r_e_a_m, _i_n_t _m_o_d_e);

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ffwwiiddee() function determines the orientation of the stream pointed at
     by _s_t_r_e_a_m.

     If the orientation of _s_t_r_e_a_m has already been determined, ffwwiiddee() leaves
     it unchanged.  Otherwise, ffwwiiddee() sets the orientation of _s_t_r_e_a_m accord‐
     ing to _m_o_d_e.

     If _m_o_d_e is less than zero, _s_t_r_e_a_m is set to byte-oriented.  If it is
     greater than zero, _s_t_r_e_a_m is set to wide-oriented.  Otherwise, _m_o_d_e is
     zero, and _s_t_r_e_a_m is unchanged.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The ffwwiiddee() function returns a value according to orientation after the
     call of ffwwiiddee(); a value less than zero if byte-oriented, a value greater
     than zero if wide-oriented, and zero if the stream has no orientation.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     ferror(3), fgetc(3), fgetwc(3), fopen(3), fputc(3), fputwc(3),
     freopen(3), stdio(3)

SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The ffwwiiddee() function conforms to ISO/IEC 9899:1999 (“ISO C99”).

